Z||000002||Steve Normington||08-09-2001||12:42 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Adam Mayer:<BR><B>what is the HP of a 3400 engine<BR>what is the stock compression ratio of a late model 3100/3400 engine?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>3400 pushrod engine<BR>3400 with iron heads = 160 hp<BR>3400 with aluminum heads = 180 hp<BR>1997 3100 engine 9.5:1<P><B>Edit</B> If the car is currently using a 2.8, then the swap should be pretty easy. Get the 3.4 from a 92-95 Camarobird and use the head from your car. If the car is FWD, you will need to drill and tap holes for the starter. If the car is RWD, no changes should be required. If the car is FI, you might need to get larger injectors and an adjustable fuel pressure regulator.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Steve Normington (edited 08-09-2001).]||||reg||1
